#! **This transcript records a known bug.** It is committed because the
#! recorded artifact IS the evidence attached to `divergences.toml`'s
#! DIV-LSP-001, and because a re-record is how anyone will notice the day it
#! gets fixed.
#!
#! `resolve/dupdef/main.lu` and its `member: true` sibling `twice.lu` are ONE
#! module (D32), and `wolf conform-run resolve/dupdef/main.lu` reports
#! `fail(E0302)` — `helper` is defined in both. Opening `main.lu` in an editor
#! publishes an EMPTY diagnostics array, which is what the record below shows:
#! the server publishes only diagnostics whose PRIMARY span lies in the
#! document being published, and this one's primary is in `twice.lu`.
#!
#! So the user sees a clean file for code that does not build. `lspconf
#! onetruth` detects this rather than mirroring the server's filter — see
#! `crates/lsp_harness/src/onetruth.rs`, the reachability comparison — and
#! reports it as KNOWN against the ledger.
#!
#! When the fix lands upstream, this transcript turns red on re-record, the
#! ledger entry goes stale and fails, and both are deliberate.
name      diagnostics/cross-file-e0302
profile   minimal

initialize
open      resolve/dupdef/main.lu
wait      diagnostics resolve/dupdef/main.lu
shutdown
